var e={title:`About`,blocks:[{kind:`html`,html:`<h1>About</h1>
<p>bootlace brings Bootstrap 6 to Angular as a component library with modern Angular APIs. The
markup and CSS come from Bootstrap. Behaviour, accessibility and the APIs are built for Angular.</p>
<h2 id="principles"><a href="#principles">Principles</a></h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bootstrap 6 CSS, nothing on top.</strong> Components render Bootstrap 6 markup and classes and are
themed with Bootstrap&#39;s own tokens, so Bootstrap themes, dark mode and utilities keep working. The
few things Bootstrap lacks, such as the layout shell and icon themes, are built on the same tokens.</li>
<li><strong>Modern Angular.</strong> Standalone components, signal inputs and models, and <code>OnPush</code> change
detection. Each component has its own entry point, so apps only bundle what they use.</li>
<li><strong>Accessible by default.</strong> Each component follows the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices for its
pattern, covering roles, keyboard support and focus. Its docs page has accessibility notes.</li>
<li><strong>Safe on the server.</strong> Every component can be rendered with Angular SSR and prerendered.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="credits"><a href="#credits">Credits</a></h2>
<p>The docs design and many component APIs follow <a href="https://taiga-ui.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Taiga UI</a>. Component
behaviour also draws on <a href="https://ng-bootstrap.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ng-bootstrap</a> and
<a href="https://ng.ant.design" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NG-ZORRO</a>. Icons are generated from ByteDance&#39;s
<a href="https://github.com/bytedance/IconPark" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IconPark</a>. <a href="/information/licensing">Licensing</a> gives the
licence of each.</p>
<h2 id="status"><a href="#status">Status</a></h2>
<p>The project is pre-release and built against <code>bootstrap@6.0.0-alpha.1</code>. Releases follow semantic
versioning: 0.x prereleases can change APIs, and 1.0 ships once Bootstrap 6 is stable. The
<a href="/information/changelog">Changelog</a> lists each release, and the
<a href="/information/migration-guide">Migration guide</a> gives upgrade steps for breaking changes.</p>
<h2 id="source"><a href="#source">Source</a></h2>
<p>The source, issues and discussions are on
<a href="https://github.com/Angular-Bootstrap-Project/angular-bootstrap" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. Contributions are welcome.
The repository&#39;s README explains how to build and test the packages.</p>
`}]};export{e as CONTENT};